### Field conventions

{{#if capabilities.logs.streams}}
Field names per stream live in the cross-reference table below; record here only each stream's casing rules and any field that silently returns zero when queried the obvious way.

- **<stream>**: <casing rules, query traps>
{{else}}
Each stream may name the same concept differently. Per stream: the identity field and its casing, the environment field and its values, the time field, the free-text field, any field that silently returns zero when queried the obvious way.

- **<stream>**: <identity field (casing)> · <environment field (values)> · <time field> · <free-text field> · <silent-zero fields>
{{/if}}

{{#if capabilities.logs.streams}}
### Field cross-reference

The same concept can sit under a different field per stream, and a wrong field reads as a false zero. Resolve the field by stream before querying.

| Concept | {{#each capabilities.logs.streams}}`{{ this.name }}` | {{/each}}
|---|{{#each capabilities.logs.streams}}---|{{/each}}
| service identity |{{#each capabilities.logs.streams}} <field> |{{/each}}
| environment |{{#each capabilities.logs.streams}} <field and values> |{{/each}}
| log text |{{#each capabilities.logs.streams}} <field> |{{/each}}
| timestamp |{{#each capabilities.logs.streams}} <field and format> |{{/each}}
| severity |{{#each capabilities.logs.streams}} <field and values> |{{/each}}
| trace correlation |{{#each capabilities.logs.streams}} <field, or none> |{{/each}}

{{else}}
### Field cross-reference

The same concept can sit under a different field per stream, and a wrong field reads as a false zero. Resolve the field by stream before querying.

| Concept | `<stream A>` | `<stream B>` |
|---|---|---|
| service identity | <field> | <field> |
| environment | <field and values> | <field and values> |
| log text | <field> | <field> |
| timestamp | <field and format> | <field and format> |
| severity | <field and values> | <field and values> |
| trace correlation | <field, or none> | <field, or none> |

{{/if}}
### Wrong-field traps

Before reading a zero as absence, run a control query that must return something: a scan with no control cannot tell "really none" from "my query is broken".

- A presence check covers every stream a service can log to; one service may log to several, so a zero in one stream is not absence.
- <symptom> — <cause>; <fix>.

