## Database schema

Schema is code-checkable: table definitions, column meaning and stored-procedure bodies live in {{ capabilities.db_schema.repos_hint }}. To confirm a table, column or procedure, find which repo holds that database (map below), then grep it. Do not stop at "the procedure is not in the caller's repo": configurable values such as thresholds and toggles live in the caller, but the time window and row filter are often written inside the procedure body, so read it.

| Database | Schema repo | Examples seen |
|---|---|---|
{{#if derived.db_map}}
{{#each derived.db_map}}
| {{ this.db }} | `{{ this.repo }}` | <tables or procedures worth knowing> |
{{/each}}
{{else}}
| <database> | <repo> | <tables or procedures worth knowing> |
{{/if}}

- When several versions of a procedure coexist, read the highest.
- Record location pointers (which meaning lives in which table and column), never data values: values change, pointers do not.
{{/if}}
